# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ApexSpider Innovation — Environment Variables
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env to version control.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── EmailJS Configuration (Client-Side Email Service) ──
# Get your credentials from: https://dashboard.emailjs.com
# 1. Create an EmailJS account
# 2. Add an email service (Gmail, Outlook, etc.)
# 3. Create an email template with variables: {{name}}, {{email}}, {{projectType}}, {{message}}
# 4. Copy your Service ID, Template ID, and Public Key below
# NOTE: VITE_* variables are intentionally public — EmailJS public keys are
#       designed for client-side use. Configure domain restrictions in your
#       EmailJS dashboard for production security.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key_here

# ── Error Tracking (Optional — Sentry) ──────────────────
# If you want production error tracking:
# 1. Create a free account at https://sentry.io
# 2. Create a new "React" project
# 3. Copy the DSN from: Project Settings → Client Keys (DSN)
# 4. Run: npm install @sentry/react
# 5. Activate the real implementation in src/utils/errorTracking.js
# Leave blank or unset to run without error tracking (safe default).

VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
